{"study_accession":"PRJNA1266109","secondary_study_accession":"SRP587447","title":"Free-floating Long-term Vascularized Mesenchymal Organoids [RNA-seq]","description":"The vasculature is essential for tissue function and pathology. Spheroid co-cultures of endothelial and mesenchymal stem/stromal cells (MSCs) form consistent structures, but the vascular components are short-lived. iPSC-derived vascular organoids can establish complex vasculature but often have cell heterogeneous variable maturation and low reproducibility. We presents consistently-formed, free-floating, long-term Vascularized Mesenchymal Organoids (VMOs), formed by co-culturing human umbilical vein endothelial cells (HUVECs) and MSCs in a pre-gelled minimal Matrigel scaffold. We studied organoid dynamics over 60 days culture time and used spheroids cultured for 14 days as control. Overall design: RNA was extracted from pooled samples (organoids) cultured for 3, 14, 28 and 60 days respectively. RNA was also extracted from day 14 spheroids (HUVEC + MSC no ECM scaffold)","pubmed":"41568151","geo_series":"","n_samples":4,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN48720989","study_accession":"PRJNA1266109","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"Spheroid Day 14 - D","description":"Spheroid Day 14 - D","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8998339","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-12-21","attributes":[["source_name","Human Umbilical Vein Endothelial Cells"],["cell_type","Bone Marrow Mesenchymal Stem Cell"],["cell_type","Human Umbilical Vein Endothelial Cells"],["treatment","14 days culture time no Matrigel"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR33691275","experiment_accession":"SRX28916941","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 2000","read_count":36255406,"base_count":7323592012,"first_public":"2025-12-21","experiment_title":"NextSeq 2000 sequencing: GSM8998339: Spheroid 